Changelog::kv
  created: 2022-04-07T00:22:53Z
Created Apr 06, 2022, 08:22PM::md.update
Summary::md.summary
  I avoided having explicit layers as it makes it harder to think about things, but I find myself wanting to have certain things that go under the gridlines. For example:

  * Images (slap down a map)
  * Rectangles
  * Shapes
  * Rubble
  * Etc.

  Couple of ways to implement this:

  1. Give all objects a layer attribute.
  2. Make background a flag
  3. Duplicate the relevant objects (have a background version).

  Option 1 is the “cleanest” to implement, but adds the user interface complication of the notion of a background.

  I guess I could do option 1 but have the interface be like 2 or 3.

  I don’t really love any of these to be honest. They all seem kind of crappy. It’s nice to not have to think about layers as a user.
